{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Lifecycle - Policy - Okta Policy Deleted",
	"Description": "An Okta policy was deleted. Deleting a policy removes whatever protection it enforced, so an adversary who has reached the admin console may delete an MFA or sign-on policy to weaken authentication before moving on.\n\nEvent type: policy.lifecycle.delete\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/defense_evasion_okta_attempt_to_delete_okta_policy/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/blob/main/rules/integrations/okta/defense_evasion_okta_attempt_to_delete_okta_policy.toml\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
